  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A rapid widening of US sovereign credit spreads is interpreted by regional adversaries and proxies as reduced US fiscal resilience and political will to sustain high-cost responses, prompting them to increase kinetic pressure (more strikes and probes) to exploit perceived deterrence gaps.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
