<edge source="eastasia_alliance_strain::military_drill_scope" target="israel_region_escalation::deployment_density" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">Larger and longer military exercises directly bring additional ships, aircraft, and ground units into the theater and hold them in proximity to potential flashpoints, increasing local force concentration.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">eastasia_alliance_strain</data>
  <data key="d39">israel_region_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eastasia_alliance_strain::military_drill_scope" target="israel_region_escalation::deconflict_effectiveness" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Complex, overlapping drills create temporary airspace/sea restrictions and unplanned interactions that overwhelm or bypass routine contact channels, degrading the practical effectiveness of deconfliction mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">eastasia_alliance_strain</data>
  <data key="d39">israel_region_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eastasia_alliance_strain::military_drill_scope" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_force_strength" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Larger or longer joint and unilateral drills in East Asia tie up forward-deployed combat units, carrier/air assets and rapid-reaction reserves, reducing the pool of readily deployable combat-capable forces that could be shifted to reinforce operations related to the Russia‑Ukraine war.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">eastasia_alliance_strain</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eastasia_alliance_strain::military_drill_scope" target="us_debt_bond_stress::bond_market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Larger, prolonged military exercises raise intraday volatility and margin requirements in fixed‑income markets, prompting dealers to shrink inventories and widening bid‑ask spreads, thereby reducing Treasury market liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">eastasia_alliance_strain</data>
  <data key="d39">us_debt_bond_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eastasia_alliance_strain::military_drill_scope" target="us_iran_confront::chokepoint_throughput" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Larger or more frequent naval and air exercises conducted near maritime chokepoints lead authorities and commercial operators to close lanes, reroute tankers, or delay transits, directly reducing short‑term throughput.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">eastasia_alliance_strain</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confront</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eastasia_alliance_strain::deterrence_credibility" target="eastasia_alliance_strain::provocative_action_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
