<edge source="israel_region_escalation::deconflict_effectiveness" target="eastasia_alliance_strain::escalation_propensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved deconfliction in the Israel theater reduces cross-command uncertainty and information frictions; conversely, a drop in deconfliction effectiveness erodes shared incident‑handling practices and trust among forces that operate across theaters, increasing the systemic tendency for incidents in East Asia to escalate.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">israel_region_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">eastasia_alliance_strain</data>
</edge>
<edge source="israel_region_escalation::deconflict_effectiveness" target="russia_ukraine_war::logistics_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved deconfliction between regional and external militaries reduces risks to commercial and military sea/air corridors (e.g., Red Sea, Gulf approaches), directly restoring routing certainty and throughput for munitions and supplies bound for Europe and Ukraine, while degraded deconfliction lowers that throughput.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">israel_region_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="israel_region_escalation::deconflict_effectiveness" target="us_iran_confront::military_tension" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">More effective deconfliction protocols and real-time communications reduce misidentification and accidental engagements between US and Iranian units, directly lowering the intensity of military escalation.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">israel_region_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confront</data>
</edge>
