<edge source="israel_region_escalation::deployment_density" target="eastasia_alliance_strain::military_drill_scope" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher concentration of deployed assets near the Israel theater leads the U.S. and regional partners to reallocate and pre-position remaining forces in the Indo‑Pacific and to enlarge the scale/duration of scheduled joint exercises there as a compensatory reassurance and deterrence measure.</data>
  <data key="d37">1-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">israel_region_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">eastasia_alliance_strain</data>
</edge>
<edge source="israel_region_escalation::deployment_density" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_force_strength" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher concentration of US/NATO naval and air assets in the Eastern Mediterranean and Gulf to respond to an Israel escalation forces temporary redeployment of ready units away from Europe, reducing the pool of combat-capable forces available to reinforce operations in the Russia–Ukraine theatre.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">israel_region_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="israel_region_escalation::deployment_density" target="us_iran_confront::military_tension" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater concentration and proximity of US and allied naval/air/military assets near Iranian forces and key waterways increases the probability of close encounters and reciprocal force-posturing, elevating US-Iran military tension.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">israel_region_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confront</data>
</edge>
